  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A water cooler of storage capacity 120 litres can cool water at constant rate of P watts. In a closed circulation system (as shown schematically in the figure), the water from the cooler is used to cool an external device that generates constantly 3 kW of heat (thermal load). The temperature of water fed into the device cannot exceed <math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi></math> and the entire stored 120 litres of water is initially cooled to <math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi></math> . The entire system is thermally insulated. The minimum value of P (in watts) for which the device can be operated for 3 hours is:<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Phy_4.jpg\"/><br >(Specific heat of water is 4.2 kJ <math><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi> </mi><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and the density of water is 1000 kg <math><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> )</p>",
    "image": null
  },
